00:00:21.593 --> 00:00:37.060
Where the grocery platform's big data lives, and how it moves: blobs in object storage, static bytes through a CDN, analytics off the OLTP path in a columnar lake, and batch and streaming pipelines that stay correct through crashes and late data.

9
00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:38.961
Four labs on real tools:

10
00:00:39.241 --> 00:00:48.436
SeaweedFS (S3 API), JDK HTTP servers, PostgreSQL 16, DuckDB 1.1 and Parquet.

11
00:00:48.716 --> 00:00:54.049
L1: object storage over the S3 API with hand-written SigV4.

12
00:00:54.329 --> 00:01:03.993
Presigned upload or download, expiry and tampering (403), multipart upload with a single part retried, and content-addressed dedup.

13
00:01:05.343 --> 00:01:07.370
L2: a pull-through CDN node.

14
00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:18.423
Normalising the cache key raised the hit ratio from 57 % to 97.5 % (origin egress 953, then 23 MB).

15
00:01:18.703 --> 00:01:22.607
Request coalescing cut 400 origin requests to 1.

16
00:01:22.887 --> 00:01:32.274
Purge or versioned URLs removed 93 stale price responses, and stale-if-error served 50 of 50 requests during an origin outage.

17
00:01:32.554 --> 00:01:33.407
L3:

18
00:01:33.687 --> 00:01:36.269
OLTP versus OLAP on 10M order lines.

19
00:01:36.549 --> 00:01:43.226
An ELT step turned 754 MB of CSV into 58 MB of Parquet.

20
00:01:43.506 --> 00:01:59.186
DuckDB answered most analytical queries 3.5 to 4x faster than PostgreSQL on 2 vCPUs, with identical results, while PostgreSQL won the point lookup (0.9 ms versus 11 ms).

21
00:01:59.466 --> 00:02:04.266
Precomputing the local date during ELT made one query 7x faster.

22
00:02:05.616 --> 00:02:07.280
L4: batch and stream.

23
00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:16.691
A restartable chunked batch job was off by 5.4 crore rupees when its checkpoint was committed separately from its output, and exact otherwise.

24
00:02:16.971 --> 00:02:30.453
For streaming windows over out-of-order events, processing-time windows were 30 % exact, a 5 s watermark 43 %, and a 5 s watermark with 30 min allowed lateness 100 %.

25
