00:08:04.941 --> 00:08:05.816
Part 2.

115
00:08:06.096 --> 00:08:07.973
Core Concepts, Beginner to Deep.

116
00:08:09.223 --> 00:08:10.141
Intuition.

117
00:08:10.421 --> 00:08:14.303
Object storage is the warehouse's back room of labelled boxes.

118
00:08:14.583 --> 00:08:16.759
You don't open a box to change one item.

119
00:08:17.039 --> 00:08:19.877
You replace the whole box (immutable objects).

120
00:08:20.157 --> 00:08:27.965
Boxes are addressed by label (key), anyone with a signed slip (presigned URL) can pick one up, and it's vast and cheap.

121
00:08:28.245 --> 00:08:37.269
A CDN is a set of small shops near every neighbourhood, stocking copies of the most popular items from the central warehouse (the origin).

122
00:08:37.549 --> 00:08:48.301
The trick is labelling: if Atta 5 kg and Atta 5 kg (from the Diwali leaflet) are shelved separately, the shop keeps running back to the warehouse (the cache key).

123
00:08:48.581 --> 00:08:52.762
OLTP versus OLAP is the billing counter versus the monthly stock-take:

124
00:08:54.112 --> 00:08:57.995
The counter needs one customer's cart, fast (rows, indexes).

125
00:08:58.275 --> 00:09:02.840
The stock-take needs a total per category across every shelf (columns, scans).

126
00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:08.112
Doing the stock-take at the billing counter during rush hour is the Monday morning incident.

127
00:09:08.392 --> 00:09:13.619
Batch versus stream is counting the day's takings after closing versus a live tally:

128
00:09:13.899 --> 00:09:19.616
The live tally is fast but must handle receipts that arrive late (event time and watermarks).

129
00:09:19.896 --> 00:09:26.168
The after-closing count is exact, but only if you can restart it without counting a drawer twice (checkpoints).

130
00:09:27.518 --> 00:09:29.097
Blob and object storage.

131
00:09:29.377 --> 00:09:30.721
Here is a quick table:

132
00:09:31.001 --> 00:09:42.222
Block storage (EBS), and File storage (EFS or NFS), and Object storage (S3, GCS, Azure Blob, MinIO, SeaweedFS, Ceph RGW).

133
00:09:42.502 --> 00:09:43.270
Unit.

134
00:09:43.550 --> 00:09:45.257
Block storage (EBS):

135
00:09:45.537 --> 00:09:46.795
Block on a volume.

136
00:09:47.075 --> 00:09:49.614
